# What `gcloud builds submit .` uploads for the Cloud Run image (editions/gcp/deploy/deploy.ps1 / deploy.sh).
# Everything in .gitignore stays local (generated worlds, .venv, caches, models); so do the parts of the
# repository the image does not use. The Dockerfile reads: pyproject.toml uv.lock README.md LICENSE src ui
# .streamlit data/docs data/samples (the voice-intake samples) evals editions/gcp.
# gitignore syntax: a pattern without a leading "/" matches at ANY depth ("docs/" would also drop data/docs), so
# every top-level directory below is anchored with "/". tests/gcp/test_gcp_one_command_deploy.py checks the upload.
# data/docs/index (the docs search index; gitignored by data/docs/.gitignore, which gcloud does not read: only the
# root .gitignore is included below) IS uploaded when the deploying machine built it, so the image carries it
# (python -m wapsi.search.bake); its extracted full texts (index/text/) are not needed at run time.
.gcloudignore
.git
.gitignore
#!include:.gitignore
/.claude/
/.agents/
/.cache/
/.github/
/tests/
/pitch/
/scripts/
/docs/
/editions/amd/
/data/golden/
/data/docs/raw/
/data/docs/index/text/
